      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We describe a patient with a history of early morning chest pain who developed ST segment elevation during a treadmill exercise test. Severe coronary artery stenosis was identified initially and was relieved after intracoronary administration of nitroglycerin. A history of vasospastic angina in this patient facilitated prompt diagnosis."},
